# DashboardRenderer keeps the header wrapper as a full blank grid row when the console chrome suppresses its content

`packages/plugin-dashboard/src/DashboardRenderer.tsx:949` (origin/main):

```tsx
const headerSection = schema.header && (
  <div className="col-span-full mb-4">
    {!hideHeaderText && schema.header.showTitle !== false && headerTitle && (<h2 …>…</h2>)}
    {!hideHeaderText && schema.header.showDescription !== false && schema.description && (<p …>…</p>)}
    {schema.header.actions && schema.header.actions.length > 0 && (…)}
  </div>
);
```

The wrapper renders whenever `schema.header` is declared; each **child** is additionally gated on `!hideHeaderText` (set when the console page chrome already renders the dashboard's title/description). With the chrome present and no `header.actions`, every child evaluates falsy — and the wrapper still renders.

## Measured consequence (HotCRM `executive_dashboard`, console route)

```html
<div class="col-span-full mb-4"></div>   <!-- height 64px, zero children -->
```

The empty div spans the grid and claims a full grid row (row sizing gives it 64px) plus `mb-4`; total dead band above the filter bar ≈ 190 CSS px. HotCRM declares `header: { showTitle: true, showDescription: true }` on all five dashboards — correct authoring, since a standalone embed renders it — so **every** dashboard page in the flagship exemplar opens with a blank band. The app author has no lever: removing `header` trades a renderer bug for lost standalone behaviour.

## Expected

The header wrapper costs zero pixels when all its content is suppressed. Compute the children first and render the wrapper only if any survive — e.g. gate `headerSection` on `(!hideHeaderText && (title-visible || description-visible)) || actions.length > 0` — or equivalent. A regression test should pin: `header` declared + `hideHeaderText` + no actions ⇒ no wrapper in the DOM; and the standalone embed (`hideHeaderText` false) still renders title/description.
